body:
- **External inputs:** `inputs#I1` — the phase directive: the 2026-10-19 driver-side trim instance on claude 2.1.296
  (a send ending in a space submitted trimmed, filed `human`, exit 13, every later send refused until a `release`);
  no live start without asking; no mutation run; controls under `--timeout 120`; the operator away

2. **The predicate's cases (the same file's `#[cfg(test)]` module).**
   - An rstest table `submitted_form_takes_a_trailing_run_the_cli_trims`. Each case holds:
     - a typed `"go "`, `"go\t"`, `"go  \t "`, `"go\n "` and `"two\nlines "`, each with its trimmed form;
     - the equal pair `"go"` / `"go"`.
   - An rstest table `submitted_form_refuses_every_other_difference`. Each case reads false:
     - a leading run (`" go"` / `"go"`);
     - a run kept and lengthened (`"go"` / `"go "`, `"go"` / `"go\n"`);
     - an inner change (`"a b"` / `"a  b"`);
     - a non-ASCII space (`"go\u{a0}"` / `"go"`);
     - an empty submitted text for a whitespace-only typed text (`"  "` / `""`);
     - a case change (`"Go "` / `"go"`).
   - One `proptest!` property at 512 cases, `submitted_form_prop_a_trailing_run_claims_and_a_leading_one_does_not`:
     - for any `T` that ends in no `SUBMIT_TRIM` character, and any non-empty run `Q` of them, `(T + Q, T)` is true;
     - `(Q + T, T)` is false.
   - Keeps tests S3 (naming), S4 (synthetic text), S1 (no state).

- (arch, security) A driver's send whose text ends in whitespace the CLI trims is confirmed as the driver's own. The
  wheel stays with the driver and the send succeeds, and a refused character is still refused, never removed.
  Proved by:
  - the unit cases (`cargo nextest run --features fake-agent --bin viola --no-fail-fast -E "test(/run::send::/)"`);
  - the booted case (`cargo nextest run --features fake-agent --test cli_send --no-fail-fast -E "test(=send_ending_in_whitespace_the_cli_trims_is_read_back_and_keeps_the_wheel)"`);
  - the refused-character rules, green in `cargo nextest run --features fake-agent --test cli_send --test channel_paste_validation --test cli_fake_agent --test contract_fake_agent_drift --no-fail-fast`;
  - the `trail-trim` control reading `holds` (`matrix#v2-18`).

- Research files inspected:
  - `src/run/send/slot.rs`, `src/run/send.rs`, `src/run/send/test_support.rs`, `src/run/send/relabel.rs`,
    `src/run/send/classify.rs`, `src/run/wheel.rs`, `src/run/gate.rs`;
  - `crates/viola-agent-claude/src/hook.rs`, `crates/viola-agent-claude/src/screen.rs`;
  - `src/bin/viola-fake-agent.rs`, `tests/cli_send.rs`, `fixtures/claude/*/UserPromptSubmit.*.json`.

- Graph impact:
  - `claim` @ `src/run/send/slot.rs:193`, its one caller `append_hook_event`;
  - `turn_running` @ `src/run/send.rs:103` and `:128`.
